---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Warning Cry — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 81"
  description="Chullin 81: play the witness. Eight knives, one day — cry the hatra'ah (forewarning) only at the moment, and about the charge, that makes the lashes stick. Hatra'at safek is no warning at all."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0c0a11] !text-[#eae3d2]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#2b2438] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#191327]/80 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#c08b3f]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#dfa14e]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 81 · 2026-07-20
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">📢 The Warning Cry</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-2xl !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">הַתְרָאַת סָפֵק לֹא שְׁמָהּ הַתְרָאָה</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">
        No Jewish court flogs a man who was not <em>warned</em>. In the breath before the knife falls,
        a witness must cry the charge — and today's daf keeps asking when that cry can even work.
        If, at the moment you shout, the violation might still evaporate — blood never sprinkled,
        meat never permitted — your warning is only a doubt, and
        <span class="frank !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">הַתְרָאַת סָפֵק לֹא שְׁמָהּ הַתְרָאָה</span> —
        <em>an uncertain warning is no warning at all</em> (81a:13).
        <strong class="!text-[#eae3d2]">Today, you are the witness.</strong>
        Eight slaughters, one day. Cry only when the lashes will stick.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Bench rules ============ -->
      <div class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#141109] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">rules of the bench — read before you shout</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🗣️ The lash needs a cry</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">Lashes land only if the transgressor was forewarned in the moment before the act. Silence at the right moment sets him free.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">❓ No doubtful cries</p>
            <p class="frank mt-1 text-sm leading-snug !text-[#cfc4a4]" dir="rtl" lang="he">הַתְרָאַת סָפֵק לֹא שְׁמָהּ הַתְרָאָה</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">If, when you cry, the violation might never come true, the court strikes your warning (81a:13).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">1️⃣ The first knife is free</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]"><em>Oto v'et beno</em> — "it and its offspring" (Lev. 22:28) — is only ever broken by the <strong class="!text-[#eae3d2]">second</strong> slaughter of the day.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">⚖️ Know your bench</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">Rabbi Shimon: a slaughter that permits no eating is <em>no slaughter</em>. The Rabbis: it counts anyway. And a graver penalty can swallow the lash. Read the plaque above each case.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Game ============ -->
      <div id="game-area"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#16121d] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">learn the real daf</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">
          Chullin 81 runs Rabbi Shimon's principle — unfit slaughter is no slaughter — through sacrificial
          animals, burnt offerings, idolatrous knives and a stabbed calf, and it all keeps landing on the
          forewarning. It ends mid-question: Rabbi Shimon himself says a slaughtered
          <a class="!text-[#dfa14e] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.81b.13">red heifer can contract food-impurity</a>
          "since it had a moment fit for consumption" — so was its slaughter fit after all? Tomorrow's daf wrestles with it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.81a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#c08b3f]/40 bg-[#c08b3f]/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e] hover:bg-[#c08b3f]/20">Chullin 81 on Sefaria →</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.81a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Rashi (×41)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.81a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Steinsaltz (×28)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Chullin.81a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Rabbeinu Gershom (×19)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin.81a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Tosafot (×5)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank {
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .sun-dot { transition: cx 0.6s ease, cy 0.6s ease; }
      .fade-in { animation: fadeIn 0.35s ease both; }
      @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

    // ---- The docket: every ruling below is sourced to Chullin 81 ----
    // Each case: moments of the day. At each moment the player holds or cries.
    // cries: the cry buttons offered at that moment (usually one; the idolatry
    // cases offer a choice of charge). ok:true = the warning sticks (lashes).
    const STRIKE_FIRST = {
      ok: false,
      head: 'Struck — the first knife of the day',
      body: 'The court strikes your warning. "It and its offspring" is only ever violated by the second slaughter of a day; the first transgresses nothing, and there is no charge to warn him of.',
    };
    const STRIKE_ALTAR = {
      ok: false,
      head: 'Struck — that is a priest doing a mitzva',
      body: 'The court strikes your warning. The priest dashing blood against the altar is performing the service, not a transgression. Save your breath for the knife.',
    };

    const CASES = [
      {
