            }],
          },
        ],
        hold: {
          ok: false,
          head: 'He walks free — but this bench counts the altar as an eater',
          body: 'In Rabbi Yoḥanan’s court the olah’s slaughter was fit — אֲכִילַת מִזְבֵּחַ שְׁמָהּ אֲכִילָה, the altar’s consumption is consumption (81b:2–3) — so a cry at the mother’s knife would have stuck. Same day, different sage, opposite verdict: that is the machloket.',
        },
      },
      {
        title: 'The Torn Calf, Before the Rabbis',
        he: 'נִמְצָא אֶחָד מֵהֶם טְרֵפָה',
        court: 'The Rabbis of the Mishnah presiding',
        cast: '🐄 the mother — healthy, chullin · 🐮 her calf — visibly a tereifa (mauled; its meat can never be permitted)',
        ref: 'Chullin 81b:4 (Mishnah)',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.81b.4',
        moments: [
          {
            t: 'dawn', icon: '🔪',
            text: 'He slaughters the healthy mother. First of the day.',
