                label: '📢 Cry: "Idolatry!"',
                ok: false,
                head: 'The graver charge swallows your cry',
                body: 'Warned of the idolatry, he now faces the death penalty — and one who bears the greater punishment does not also receive the lesser. The capital case swallows the lashes of oto v’et beno; your flogging never happens (81b:6–8).',
              },
              {
                label: '📢 Cry both charges!',
                ok: false,
                head: 'The graver charge swallows the lesser',
                body: 'Both cries were heard — so the death penalty for idolatry stands, and it swallows the lashes. He receives only the greater punishment (81b:6–8).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
        hold: {
          ok: false,
          head: 'He leaves the grove unwarned and unpunished',
          body: 'In Rabbi Yoḥanan’s court a cry of oto v’et beno alone — and only that — would have made the lashes stick, precisely because he was never warned of the capital crime (81b:7–8). Silence gave him everything.',
        },
      },
      {
        title: 'The Same Knife, Before Reish Lakish',
        he: 'כִּי לָא אַתְרוֹ בֵּיהּ נָמֵי פָּטוּר',
        court: 'Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish presiding',
        cast: '🐄 the mother — slaughtered for his table · 🐮 her offspring — bound for the idol’s grove',
        ref: 'Chullin 81b:8',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.81b.8',
        moments: [
          {
            t: 'dawn', icon: '🔪',
            text: 'The same day replays once more — Reish Lakish now sits on the bench. The mother falls for his table. First of the day.',
            cries: [{ label: '📢 Cry the warning!', ...STRIKE_FIRST }],
          },
          {
            t: 'afternoon', icon: '🗿',
            text: 'Again he drags the offspring toward the grove, knife out. Lashes and death hang over the same cut. What do you cry?',
            cries: [
              {
                label: '📢 Cry: "It and its offspring!"',
                ok: false,
                head: 'Struck — the shadow of the sword',
                body: 'Reish Lakish holds: since, had you warned him of the idolatry, he would be exempt from lashes — then even when you warn only of oto v’et beno he is exempt. The graver penalty shields him from the lash even unspoken (81b:8).',
              },
              {
                label: '📢 Cry: "Idolatry!"',
                ok: false,
                head: 'The capital case swallows the lash',
                body: 'Warned of the idolatry he faces death, and the greater punishment absorbs the lesser. On this bench there were never lashes to be had (81b:8).',
              },
              {
                label: '📢 Cry both charges!',
                ok: false,
